294 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 224 0 R
/E (Detecting hate speech on Vietnamese social media is difficult because hateful intent often appears implicitly through informal group references, slang, sarcasm, and indirect insinuation rather than explicit named entities. Although AmpleHate shows that modeling the relation between an utterance and its target can improve implicit hate detection, its English NER and English-oriented target categories transfer poorly to Vietnamese: on our training data, English NER finds usable targets in only about 0.09% of comments, causing the model to behave almost like a plain sentence classifier.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
