357 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 227 0 R
/E (Vietnamese hate speech often depends on informal target references such as pronouns, group nouns, and address forms. Existing datasets show the importance of target information, but ViAmpleHate does not require span-level annotation; it uses Vietnamese NER and cue banks to locate target and attack positions.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
358 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 227 0 R
/E (Contrastive Learning for Text Classification)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
359 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 227 0 R
/E (Contrastive learning helps bring same-class representations closer and push different-class representations apart. ViAmpleHate combines weighted cross-entropy with a contrastive auxiliary objective to improve separation between the frequent NON-HATE class and the rare HATE class.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
