595 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1420 0 R
/E (Offensive but not hate: profanity or insults aimed at individuals can be mistaken as HATE if attack cues are over-weighted.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
596 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1421 0 R
/E (Implicit hate: sarcasm, stereotypes, or coded language may express hate without explicit targets or attack words, so cue extraction often fails.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
597 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1422 0 R
